Testing clipboard.device
OK: clipboard.device opened
OK: CBD_CURRENTWRITEID returns a positive clip ID
OK: CBD_CURRENTREADID equals CBD_CURRENTWRITEID
OK: CMD_WRITE writes the clip
  new clip ID - base = 1
OK: CMD_UPDATE commits the clip
OK: CBD_CURRENTREADID tracks the committed clip
OK: CBD_CURRENTWRITEID tracks the committed clip
OK: CMD_READ returns the clip up to its FORM size
OK: CMD_READ past the end returns 0 bytes and ClipID -1
OK: CMD_READ reads sequential parts
OK: CMD_READ with NULL io_Data skips to the end
OK: skipped read ends at the clip end
OK: CBD_CHANGEHOOK installs hook
OK: CBD_POST assigns the next clip ID
  change hook calls = 1
  hook call: cmd=9 clip=base+2 object=io_Unit
OK: CBD_CURRENTREADID tracks the post
OK: CBD_CURRENTWRITEID tracks the post
OK: CMD_READ of a posted clip pends
OK: CBD_POST sends a SatisfyMsg on demand
  change hook calls = 1
  hook call: cmd=9 clip=base+2 object=io_Unit
OK: satisfying CMD_WRITE starts
  change hook calls = 0
OK: satisfying write uses the post ID
OK: pending CMD_READ completes with the posted data
OK: posted clip read ends at the clip end
  change hook calls = 1
  hook call: cmd=4 clip=base+2 object=io_Unit
OK: CBD_CHANGEHOOK removes hook
OK: removed change hook is not called
OK: second CBD_POST assigns the next clip ID
OK: CMD_READ of the second post pends
OK: second post sends a SatisfyMsg
OK: AbortIO aborts a pending CMD_READ
OK: the aborted post can still be satisfied
OK: RemDevice() while open sets LIBF_DELEXP and keeps the device
OK: OpenDevice() after deferred expunge clears LIBF_DELEXP
